            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why though?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tim Lee",
                        "email": "timlee660101@gmail.com",
                        "username": "timlee66"
                    },
                    "message": "There are three sensors that show unavailable when performing mfg-tool test.\n\nWe found the following in the log: the i2c driver failed to register i2c client device xdp710 at 0x11 and 0x13.\n\n```\nbmc psusensor[1035]: Failed to instantiate xdp710 at address 17 on bus 11\nbmc psusensor[1035]: Failed to instantiate xdp710 at address 19 on bus 11\nbmc kernel: i2c i2c-11: Failed to register i2c client xdp710 at 0x11 (-16)\nbmc kernel: i2c i2c-11: Failed to register i2c client xdp710 at 0x13 (-16)\n```\nWe asked WW for help to confirm whether this CONFIG_SENSORS_XDP710 is set, and found find this configuration is not set.\n```\nroot@bmc:~# zcat /proc/config.gz | grep SENSORS_XDP710\n# CONFIG_SENSORS_XDP710 is not set\n```\nAfter manually adding this kernel configuration, all sensors were reported as ok in WW test results.\n\nShould we enable this configuration into yosemite4-common.cfg instead of SoC-specific .cfg, ince sensors should be same?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes.  We should move all the required sensor configs over to the yosemite4-common.cfg file.  Please remove them from yosemite4.cfg (and yosemite4n.cfg) and put them there."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tim Lee",
                        "email": "timlee660101@gmail.com",
                        "username": "timlee66"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for your review. I have moved them to yosemite4-common.cfg file."
                }
            ],
            "files": [
